<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="639a5ab5">&lt;p&gt;
    The work product encompasses the design of each learning course, providing a detailed description, course objectives,
    length, skills and competencies fulfilled, target audience, and a sequence of topics. Consideration is also given to
    the design materials used by instructors, providing for the inclusion of resources such as instructor guides,
    participant workbooks, presentation slides, and interactive activities to support effective delivery and engagement
    during learning sessions.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="b8dc362b"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="6199ced0">&lt;p&gt;
    Collaboration with the organization Learning and Talent teams is crucial throughout the process. They provide a
    holistic view of the organization&apos;s learning culture and capability, offering valuable insights into the wider learning
    requirements. Their knowledge helps in developing learning curriculums based on the recognized learning needs,
    including CPE/CPD requirements and local office regulatory requirements.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    As part of the process, it is vital to review the organization&apos;s current learning design capability. This assessment
    validates that the design of the training materials is aligned with the organization&apos;s current learning
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="76684e68"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="ec3a0800">&lt;p&gt;
    To develop materials with the end user&apos;s experience front-of-mind and to construct materials consistently so they can
    be maintained easily if changes arise.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
